# What the source distribution carries beyond the package itself.
#
# setuptools' default sdist sweep takes `tests/test*.py` and nothing else under
# `tests/`, which ships the top-level test modules without `tests/conftest.py`
# (the session-wide network guard and the config-bundle fixtures), without the
# `tests/agentic_extraction/` and `tests/extraction/` packages, and without a
# single data fixture — a suite that cannot be collected. `recursive-include`
# ships it whole, data included, and `pythonpath = ["src"]` under
# `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` lets the unpacked sdist import what it ships.
recursive-include tests *
include CITATION.cff
global-exclude *.py[cod]
global-exclude .DS_Store
prune tests/**/__pycache__
